<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5473"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m wondering about this theory since Mrs.Otero was a devout Catholic and seemed to love children and even had orphans over for Christmas according to Charlie,yet stranger things have been known to have occured in these killings.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5473-->
<!--Post: 5474--><!--Time: 1107143309-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s not turn this into a &#34;right to life&#34; debate. The people that were murdered were fully formed, male, female, children. Already born. Living human beings. This is pure murder...not a zygote vs embroyo theological discussion. Can we have some limits to the random and off topic, neo-religious rantings? Tom?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
