<!--Post: 5507--><!--Time: 1107150449-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ummmm, ok. off topic and abortion and killing fully formed humans....two entirely separate kinds of moral dicusssions. Unless you think-like, ummmm i don&#39;t know, a moron? <BR> <BR>bodycheck - that is &#34;how in the world&#34; it is &#34;off-topic&#34;. IT IS OFF-TOPIC....HELLO?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5507-->
<!--Post: 5523--><!--Time: 1107170581-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5523"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 3:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lily - if you read the entire topic post - I think you will see that this is not a discussion about religion - or abortion - it is about a possible motive for a killer, based on the way the killings were done. <BR> <BR>I certainly do not want to get into a pro or con debate about abortion or religion here.  That would be counter-productive.   <BR> <BR>But, Lily, we know there is some sexual aspect - yet not one that causes BTK to actually rape or molest these women.  I am not suggesting BTK is like any current prolife groups - more like those in other parts of our world who adhere to things like Sharia Law, where it is honorable to kill women for indiscretions.  This is a fact.  Women have suffered the death penalty for abortions.  Research it.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m certainly NOT coming down on either side of the fence here, but BTK is NOT normal.  Normal people don&#39;t go around killing others.  Somewhere in his head - something is screwed up - royally and we can&#39;t afford to shut out some scenarios just because they bother us, personally.   <BR> <BR>If you research - you will find that there are fanatics who have targeted people over the abortion issue.  It is a strong catalyst for some.  Especially those who think of women as second-class citizens.  Please read Dr. Kelleher&#39;s profile.  He demonstrates that BTK does not think much of women AND that he needs to control.   <BR> <BR>This is just a theory - but I think it deserves some thought.  <BR> <BR>Dee - I hadn&#39;t thought of that &#40;pre or post-mortem binding&#41; but, yes, I should think that could have been determined by an autopsy.  Has the public ever had access to the autopsies? <BR> <BR>Also, Dee, you are correct that Wichita is an abortion hot-spot. Lots of activity - and an abortion doctor was actually shot there - but lived.  The group you linked to - Operation Rescue - was not in full swing at the time of the Otero murders, I believe, but there is a group of activists &#40;all nice people, as I have mentioned&#41; who should know if more radical ones lurk in the background.  In fact, I believe that the leaders of the prolife movement in Wichita have publically denounced those involved in any sort of violence.  They may have dismissed BTK at some point from their groups.   <BR> <BR>Jim - you bring up an excellent point about Mrs Otero being Catholic.  I am not aware how many practicing Catholics would find themselves in a situation &#40;if they already had enough mouths to feed&#41; and would seek an abortion.  That could definetly be the &#39;chink in the armour&#39; of my theory. <BR> <BR>The last think I want to do - is insult anyone with this theory - I am just throwing it out there since the methods of binding are so strange, and the fact BTK mastrubated on the bodies.   <BR> <BR> <BR>Bodycheck - I have to agree with you - that it would now be extremely difficult to determine if abortion was a common factor.  The women, even though that was the permissive 70&#39;s and 80&#39;s may not have mentioned it, except to a small group of close and trusted aquaintances.  But, rumors fly with wings of their own.   <BR> <BR>In my research, I found that the notorious doctor in Wichita began doing abortions in 74 at Wesley Hospital, later relocating to a clinic of his own.  A number of doctors began doing them just after it was legalized - and then most, over the years, quit due to harrassment.   <BR> <BR>Also from my research - any early abortions might have been performed by the family physician - and would have been notated as a female-procedure, a D &amp; C, likely.  So, those, might be trackable through the patient&#39;s records. <BR> <BR>However, the clinic now in operation allows false names.  Well, they say they don&#39;t.  But in my reading - I found people claimed to have given them a fake name - so searching those records would be a dead-end, probably. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
