<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5540"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 6:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->L2829 - I&#39;m always up early.  Just can&#39;t sleep...glad to know I&#39;m not alone. <BR> <BR> <BR>Scbenson2001 -   Yes there are differences between clinic bombers and serial killers - but the connection is a moral one - steeped in an ancient moral battle.  Both are murderers, however. <BR> <BR>Your quote from BTK actually backs up my theory - he assumes the PD will call him that - yet, he has offered no substantial proof - and his killing are not for sex.  We know that.   <BR> <BR>Consider Jack The Ripper.  Killing prostitutes - &#34;sinners&#34;.  He, also, wrote cryptic letters to authorities and they believe drew pictures.  His method was different - he utilized a knife - but he targeted the areas of the body where the &#34;sin&#34; had occured. <BR> <BR>Also consider the history of Gary Leon Ridgeway, the Green Belt Killer.  He was punishing &#39;sinners&#39;, too. <BR> <BR>&#60;quote&#62;&#34;Ridgway was also known to have been obsessed with prostitutes, a fixation that bordered on a love hate relationship. Neighbors knew him to constantly complain about prostitutes conducting business in his neighborhood, but at the same time he frequently took advantages of their favors. It was possible that he was torn by his uncontrollable lusts and his staunch religious beliefs. McCarthy states that according to one of his wives, he became a religious fanatic, often times crying following sermons and reading the bible. &#34;&#60;unquote&#62; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/predators/greenriver/threat_7.html?sect=2" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/predato rs/greenriver/threat_7.html?sect=2</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>If BTK tied up the males differently than he did the females - it seems to suggest some sort of motive.  And, if he tied their legs shut, did not rape them - just bound them.  I think there is another issue there. <BR> <BR>This is just a theory, guys.  I am not condeming anyone or their beliefs - or lack thereof.   <BR> <BR>But it seems like many serial killers have some sort of underlying motive that they think is justifiable. <BR> <BR>I really hope someone will know the answers to the questions posted about binding pre or post mortem. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
