<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5571"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 10:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, Tippy. You are obviously a very reasonable and nice person. Sorry I accused you of having an agenda. I am one of those that thinks the abortion-driven killers have a need to be identified and have their crimes publicized in order to further their objectives 1. Use fear and intimidation to stop women from having abortions 2. Gain hero-status with the fanatics that support them. <BR> <BR>IMO....BTK doesn&#39;t have this kind of motive. He has a need to feed his ego. Period. His ego is only fed when he has total control over a victim and then ultimately plays God with their lives. His ego now must be maintained by believing in his mind that he is so incredibly smart that the WPD, FBI, and general public can&#39;t figure out who he is. He even believes that he has &#34;handed the clues on a silver platter&#34; and we are all too stupid to find him. When he&#39;s caught...he will say exactly that. In fact, when he&#39;s caught, the only way he will be able to deal with it is to believe that he gave himself up. He won&#39;t ever believe that he was outsmarted.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
