<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5572"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 11:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lily - you may be very correct.  It is true that the criminals you speak of - are very open about their crimes and motives for killing.  And, I also think you are right about their wanting to further the cause - so they publicize it. <BR> <BR>And I also agree that BTK has an intense need to feed his ego.   <BR> <BR>And likely as not, you are also right about abortion not playing a role.  I just don&#39;t want to miss anything - overlook anything.  It keeps going through my head that mostly women were targets - they were stripped, their legs bound together and semen was found on them.  They are not all of the same race, they don&#39;t bear the same facial features, or hair color.  So much about them is diametrically opposed to the others - I was just searching for something related to the way he bound the women - that they could have in common. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m a big &#34;what if...&#34; person.  I think outloud.   <BR> <BR>A fanatical Muslim man could do that to a woman and no one would bat an eye - but here we are so insulted &#40;rightly so&#41;. <BR> <BR>I really enjoy your input on topics.  I am sorry we did not see eye to eye on this one. <BR> <BR>I do respect your opinions.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
