<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5654"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 11:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Even though I&#39;m something of a &#34;pro-lifer&#34; &#40;who would have guessed?&#41;, I appreciate the thread - it&#39;s worth throwing some brain cells at, if just as an exercise in exploring new angles.  Lily is right - if we stay off the politics we&#39;re OK.  And I appreciate what you said at the top.  Although I&#39;m with SC and Lily on this theory &#40;extremely doubtful&#41;, it does bring up a very important issue - anger.  Many of the violent anti-abortionists are driven by an OCD-like obsession, but some others are dealing &#40;or rather not dealing&#41; with extreme anger issues.  This is perhaps more akin to the honor killings mentioned, although not identical.  But it seems to apply to BTK.  Whereas many SKs seem to have a sort of neutral disregard for both their victims and the police &#40;they are basically targets or impediments&#41;, BTK seems to have more obvious and perhaps more serious anger.  Whether it is his snide comments about the victims, his sarcasm, his desire to insult the police, or his brutal treatment of the victims as Lily points out, there seems to be something beyond a simple SK turn-on going on for this guy.  This makes me suspect that he had actual interactions with the victims, albeit at a level that escaped detection by the original investigators.  He may have &#34;opened up&#34; to them in some very unfortunate way, exposing his deviance or psychosis, and was rebuffed.  It wouldn&#39;t have had to have been much - perhaps simply getting the cold shoulder when he tried to talk to a woman he had admired from afar, or met at work.  Unable to deal with the rejection in a normal way, it might have evolved as anger, grown into revenge fantasies, and finally merged with his sexual fantasies. <BR> <BR>I think your observations about the bindings are significant.  But rather than abortion &#40;distantly but directly related to sexual activity&#41;, I think he was making a statement about controlling the victims&#39; sexuality.  I think that before the crimes, the victims had been in control of their sexuality, and possibly denying it to BTK &#40;even if they never even thought about it&#41;.  Like a borderline psychopath I once knew, who was angered by victims who would attempt to exert &#34;control&#34; with their tears, I believe that BTK sees the world through BTK-colored glasses, and cannot fathom why anyone would have the right to &#34;control&#34; him by denying him what he wants, or to question his righteous anger when so denied.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5654-->
<!--Post: 5657--><!--Time: 1107258030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5657"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax - yes, I think he was definetly controlling the victims.  <BR> <BR>I just have my doubts the crimes were sexually-driven.   <BR> <BR>Crimes against women &#40;mainly&#41;have an element of revenge, of power.  We hear psychologists say that many rapes are not about sex - but power. <BR> <BR>But one thing that I think we all need to do - is look at the crime scenes, not so much the correspondence BTK has sent, although that may contain underlying clues. <BR> <BR>After reading up on many, many serial killers, one thing becomes apparent, very few do NOT molest their victims.  Serial killers are &#40;for the most part&#41; sexual deviants, like Dahmer, Bundy and others. <BR> <BR>I like your idea of &#34;controling the victim&#39;s sexuality&#34;.  I think that is true.  It was an important part of his crime. <BR> <BR>But I think we are all over-looking one issue - serial killers chose victims based on &#34;something&#34;.  There IS a connection.  Until we figure that out - we can&#39;t get past square one. <BR> <BR>Okay - maybe it&#39;s not abortion, but it&#39;s something similar.  It&#39;s something female, and it&#39;s something that has to do with reproduction, or their reproductive organs - but not in a sexual way. <BR> <BR>I think we get off base thinking he is a sexual deviant like most serial killers.  He does not fit the pattern. <BR> <BR>There is a very upsetting phenomena during wartime - the rape of the opposing side&#39;s women.  And if you study war history - you will find that all sides take part in that ancient horror.  The thought is, &#34;if you control the sexuality of the women you control the people&#34;.   <BR> <BR>Many SK&#39;s operate on a very deep level of that psychosis.  BTK doesn&#39;t.  I think it is extremely important to recognize that. <BR> <BR>He could think women are &#34;dirty&#34;.  Untouchable.  But, I don&#39;t think so.   <BR> <BR>There is a connection - a reason why he chose the victims he chose.  And it wasn&#39;t sexual.   <BR> <BR>Somewhere there is a link.  Maybe it&#39;s not abortion.  But maybe it is.  Whatever the connection is - it lies in the way the women were bound - and the difference between their bondage and the males.  <BR> <BR>Thanks for everyone who has participated on this &#39;off the wall&#39; theory.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5657-->
<!--Post: 5676--><!--Time: 1107276906-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 8:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The study of victims - victimology - is as important as studying their assailants. In BTK&#39;s instance, you are correct about their possession of some characteristic&#40;s&#41; that caught his pathology. As far as has been made known, they appeared to be clean cut, honorable with a work ethic, loving, many involved in some sort of religious life, trusting, supported by loved ones, no physical abnormalities apparent from photos, health problems unknown. I am sure that others could add more.  Sounds like the perfect woman, does it not? Perhaps the binding of the legs was to prevent them from being defiled by other men. However, the physical and emotional brutality of the crimes says that he will destroy what he wants most and cannot have. Some female somewhere that should have loved him did the unthinkable. Since he is no longer able to hurt her, he hurts substitutes. How many times can one person be killed? Just once physically, but over and over again in the heart of BTK. &#34;As a man thinketh in his heart, so is he.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5676-->
<!--Post: 5718--><!--Time: 1107301638-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5718"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie is correct in that this is sexual and sadistic. Don&#39;t rule out violent penetration though Lilymarie. He at least thought about it if in fact he didn&#39;t act upon it. He drew in a sketch sent to Anna Williams what he planned to do to her and it included probing her violently with a stick-like object that resembled a police billy club or something. You have to wonder if he actually used this on some of the other victims and the police are keeping quiet about it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5718-->
<!--Post: 5724--><!--Time: 1107304643-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5724"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 4:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That made me think about something Johno. I have yet to see anything that indicates that BTK actually used his own hands to touch the victims as he hurt/killed them. He used belts, cords, rope, &#40;a knife and a gun in the Bright&#39;s case but I think that was out of necessity&#41;. If he is a true psychopathic narcissist, he may have an aversion to physical contact - preferring to use intimidation and control tactics. In most cases of multiple victims - he used them to tie one another as much as possible. I think I saw somewhere here that they found a chair in the basement &#40;Josephine had to climb up in order to have the rope slipped around her neck? All he had to do was kick the chair away and watch?&#41; <BR> <BR>Once tied, he used various methods to asphysixiate them. &#40;My opinion...I believe in some cases, they were tied in way way that required them to keep a leg flexed to keep the cord from tightening around their neck-self asphysixiation, very slowly, while BTK watched&#41;.  <BR> <BR>If WPD would release more detail we may know this for sure but, I don&#39;t believe he has a penetration fantasy - it&#39;s another false clue to FBI/WPD, but since he objectifies the victim - he uses an object and not himself to send this message.  <BR> <BR>I think that the minutes of horrible suffering of his victims - the longer the better - is the core of his twisted psyche.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5724-->
<!--Post: 5744--><!--Time: 1107317105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5744"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 8:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie wrote : <i>&#34;I think that the minutes of horrible suffering of his victims - the longer the better - is the core of his twisted psyche.&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Hits the nail on the head and hits it hard; I couldn&#39;t agree more. I still think BTK was sexually dysfunctional &#40;was incapable of penetration&#41; but even if he wasn&#39;t, the drawing with the object insertion sent to Anna Williams is a hallmark trait of a sexual sadist. &#40;Hazelwood, <i>Dark Dreams</i>.&#41; He may not have had a penetration fantasy but the semen indicates a fantasy of some sort. My own take is that he would have raped, but was unable to. But yes, BTK&#39;s crimes were ninety percent &#40;or more&#41; control-driven than they were sex-driven <BR> <BR>Tippy, consider the EAR/ONS. At first he was the East Area Rapist, committed approximately sixty rapes before murdering. Yes, the rapes were crimes of violence <i>and</i> sex. As John Douglas has quoted Ann Burgess &#40;I think it was Burgess, not positive&#41; in defining rape, &#34;Rape is a crime of violence with sex as the weapon.&#34; It&#39;s more about control than about sex but both are seen. <BR> <BR>EAR raped. Yet he then escalated to murder. If the crime was primarily sexual, I don&#39;t understand why EAR &#40;now ONS, since he&#39;s committed his first double murder&#41; would jump from rape to rape/murder. The murders also included extensive bondage with rope, rape to completion inside the female and an overkill level of violence, in terms of what would have been lethal; his choice was almost always blunt-force trauma. &#40;A fire log was used in one attack.&#41; Rape occurred, but not before the ONS &#40;Original Night Stalker if anyone is unfamiliar; don&#39;t confuse him with Richard Ramirez; this guy, believed alive as of 1990/1991 <BR>was never caught&#41; had both victims tied up, and then murdered the husband, with a helpless wife looking on, then raped the wife, then murdered her, too. There has never been a scarier or more dangerous serial killer in this country, in my opinion. He was BTK with a &#40;very powerful&#41; vengeance. In fact, there are many similarities with BTK and if time permits, anyone interested should read the official profile, most of which isn&#39;t redacted. Click &#34;Suspect Profile.&#34; <BR><a href="http://www.ear-ons.com/index2.html" target=_top>http://www.ear-ons.com/index2.html</a> There is a thread about EAR/ONS on this board but it deserves a mention here, I believe. Anyway, if the sex, while he was still known as EAR, was enough or the primary motive, it doesn&#39;t make sense that he&#39;d begin to kill wealthy young couples in their own homes. The husband&#40;s&#41; was/were bound and he could have raped the wife and then left. He was in costume, just as he was when he was EAR. Always wore gloves. Something made him go from rape to murder. Thankfully, most serial rapists don&#39;t become serial murderers but those who do are exceptionally dangerous, even for serial killers. One reason ONS was never caught was that by the time he began murderering &#40;a minimum of ten murders are attributed to him&#41;, he was well versed in stalking, surveillance, was very evidence-conscious, was fearless&#42; and in control during the murderous assaults, struck several hundred miles apart, then returned a long while later and murder/raped again in nearby areas, and on and on. Sorry for a partial repeat but I include it because I feel that ONS is the serial murderer to study if you want to learn more about BTK. The primary differences were: ONS struck at night only; was capable of heterosexual rape to the point of completion, something BTK has never been proven to have been able to do; usually killed with blunt-force trauma as opposed to BTK&#39;s strangling or asphyxiation &#40;or stabbing but the Bright attack was cut short&#41;. <BR> <BR>Tippy you mentioned something about BTK and females and something about women which makes BTK kill in the fashion he does. I agree there could be a form of &#34;judgment&#34; on BTK&#39;s part. Not about abortion, but I respect your opinions, always have, but maybe something more basic: A true hatred of women, period. This is common among serial killers. You also mention something interesting, <i>&#34;I think we get off base thinking he is a sexual deviant like most serial killers. He does not fit the pattern.</i> I&#39;m probably lost in semantics, but I don&#39;t see how it can be said that BTK is not a sexual deviant. However I agree with you about most serial killers committing sexual acts upon their victims. Quite on the button there. Let me say, not trying to cause any problem here, that there have been some serial killers of note who didn&#39;t sexually attack their victims in any traditional sense. Some are: BTK, Zodiac, Jack The Ripper, The Texarkana Phantom, some of the Santa Rosa coed murders, <i>possibly</i> H.H. Holmes, whom BTK mentions &#40;reports conflict&#41;, Belle Gunness, David Berkowitz, and some more. But the Bundy&#39;s, Gacy&#39;s, etc., are more the rule than the exception, certainly. <BR> <BR>The women being tied differently than the men. Only BTK knows with certainty. I see it simply as BTK&#39;s disgust with &#40;ie. fear of&#41; women.  <BR> <BR>The female reproductive organs/some relation to BTK which you posit. This is a very good observation. Again, I would tend to interpret it merely as anti-female. There would also be something Freudian here, in terms of Mommy, as was mentioned. But I&#39;ll let a Freudian say what.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
