<!--Post: 5770--><!--Time: 1107361254-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5770"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 8:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, don&#39;t worry about long posts - I always enjoy every word you write. You have such knowledge and insight.  I really appreciate the time you take to comment. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m a little embarrassed to mention that I do not understand how a man could be unable to penetrate, sexually, and yet still leave semen at the scene.  I&#39;m not sure I really want to go into that, however.  I blush easily. <BR> <BR>You may be very correct that abortion does not play a role - and I knew it was a long shot going in, hence the &#34;off the wall&#34; label.  But I strongly feel the &#39;judgement&#39; or &#39;punishment&#39; issue is at the root of BTK&#39;s killings and not sexual deviance. <BR> <BR>I think that it is the sexually-driven killers that usually do not stop killing, but I may be very wrong. <BR> <BR>Perhaps it is easier for a killer who feels he is meting out &#34;justice&#34; to quit, he could have a change of heart that would have no effect if he were driven by sexual rage. <BR> <BR>I think Vicki Wegerly is a good case in point.  From what I read - the likely window of time in which her murder occured, was approx 15 minutes, and I don&#39;t think any sperm was found there.  Of course, they may have just missed it.  <BR> <BR>But if sex-driven assumptions are correct - then Wegerly - a late killing - was a failure on his part.  Taking into consideration that he had to subdue her, tie her up - and then strangle her - his middle initial &#34;T for Torture&#34; didn&#39;t really apply.  Although I am sure it was a horrific nightmare for her - there was not the kind of torture seen in other SK&#39;s crimes.   <BR> <BR>And, no mention of semen.  Why go to all the trouble to pinpoint and track a victim - if the killing is sexually driven and then not complete his warped act?   <BR> <BR>I just can&#39;t help thinking that it is something else.  Something more &#34;punishment&#34; driven.   <BR> <BR>I know BTK sent that awful drawing with the club used in a violent manner - but, as with all of his messages, I find them lacking in real clues.  Instead, I think he purposefully uses them as a &#39;distraction&#39; from what the physical evidence might show. <BR> <BR>You are way ahead of me in knowing, and understanding, the nature of these killers, but it strikes me that if a killer gets some sort of sexual satisfaction from their crimes that the need would intensify - not abate.  Yet, Wegerly suffers less than &#40;we suppose&#41; the Otero&#39;s did. <BR> <BR>I am not saying with any certanity that abortion is a factor - but I am not totally dismissing it either. <BR> <BR>He chose those victims for a reason.  If we find the reason - I think we find him. <BR> <BR>Just my thoughts. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5770-->
<!--Post: 5771--><!--Time: 1107362041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5771"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 8:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t forget the &#39;Madonna-Wh---&#39; issue that many men face with females. They want to do the deed but cannot because of their view of the female as sacred. Yet, they despise her in some way. I know someone &#40;not me&#41; who dated a man who hated his mother because she had sex with his father. DUH! Again, women present an approach-avoidance conflict for BTK. Since BTK admitted being mystified by this compulsion that has gripped him, he may not be clear on it either. We will never know until he is apprehended. Clinicians will be taking a number and standing in line to see him. Maybe even Dr. Mould.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5771-->
<!--Post: 5795--><!--Time: 1107381983-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5795"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 2:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, I thought they had DNA from the Wegerle scene. Hmm. Perhaps, as it was 1986, and DNA was more in the news, BTK cleaned up after himself or possibly used a condom. I don&#39;t know, I&#39;ve read conflicting things about the Wegerle attack.  <BR> <BR>I think we&#39;re more on the same page than not. I also believe any sexual aspect takes a back seat to the control, violence and killing. The sex, in the form of masturbation, is there but not the primary reason anyone was attacked, IMO. Nor is your theory off the wall. This guy&#39;s goal was to live out a fantasy he played in his mind countless times, most of the fantasy being about binding and controlling and prowling through the house and staring into terrified eyes and so forth but I base this on other sexually sadistic offenders. Everyone&#39;s a little different. <BR> <BR>If BTK only had 15 minutes at the Wegerle scene, that <i>is</i> something I didn&#39;t know. <BR> <BR>Differing opinions? Here&#39;s my take on Ted Bundy. I don&#39;t believe that Bundy murdered because he had been rejected by his ideal woman, and this rejection was so catastrophic to Bundy&#39;s ego it launched Ted on his infamous series of killings. It played a role in deepening and galvanizing what was already there, in my opinion. It&#39;s also been widely speculated that Bundy had murdered before his fateful rejection. To me, the rejection scenario as primary cause for years of coast-to-coast killing has a bit too much of a fairy tale/Greek myth quality to it to be entirely realistic. I mention this also because the look-alike victim thing, it&#39;s not there with all of Bundy&#39;s victims. I grew up in the 1970s and that hairstyle was the one girls/young women wore. That most victims were 5&#39;1&#34; to 5&#39;5&#34; and not overweight I think was more a matter of having a lighter weighing body to dispose of than anythng else. Bundy also is overrated concerning his criminal acumen, IMO. Escaping incarceration twice is impressive but that also means being arrested twice. Two arrests - and one of them ridiculous, the one when Bundy, in his VW Bug, tried to outrun the Utah sheriff only to be pulled over and then immediately lie about being in the area because he&#39;d seen a drive-in movie, which of course he couldn&#39;t name - do not become one I&#39;d call a &#34;brilliant,&#34; or even &#34;genius&#34; killer. The death row interviews with Bundy, that book, is much closer to the mark than Ann Rule&#39;s still excellent work, I think. My view of Bundy is probably a minority one. So be it. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR>Back to Wichita, who knows with certainty? BTK and no one else. Your point about Roe V. Wade as at least turning up the heat a little, in a general sense, in BTK&#39;s mind I find entirely plausible - the feminist movement may have had an even larger impact. Or perhaps no impact at all. BTK is clever criminal, yet I don&#39;t see societal issues being a strong, driving force in his crimes. But I can only guess.  <BR> <BR>Teardrop, that&#39;s a good point. I think it&#39;s a minority of men who fall into that category but BTK may well be one of them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5795-->
<!--Post: 5812--><!--Time: 1107390060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5812"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 4:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippi -- I agree that binding the women at the knees should make people think that there&#39;s some type of motive for the murders behind it.  However, I do not think the connection between these women is abortion.  I&#39;m completely against abortion, but I do not see it as a motive for murder in this case &#40;in this case&#41;!!!  Perhaps,BTK does not rape  the women because he is not physically able to do so!  Through the pleasures of his sadistic murders his able to achieve an orgasm.  Maybe the binding of the women&#39;s knees was a sign of his own inferiority.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5812-->
<!--Post: 5867--><!--Time: 1107429701-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5867"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that including the abortion angle is a stretch.  Its known that he tied the legs together at the knees...beyond that it could be a number of things...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5867-->
<!--Post: 5892--><!--Time: 1107446604-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5892"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 8:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy I do believe that you are on to something. There has to be a link from BTK to his victims. What could it be?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5892-->
<!--Post: 6075--><!--Time: 1107527129-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6075"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I forgot to mention in regards to the question of BTK&#39;s murders being sexual in nature, that a good clue can be found in his letter about the vian murder.&#34;I was going to tape the boys and put plastic bags over there head like I did Joseph and Shirley. And then hang the girl. God Oh God what a sexual relief this would have been.&#34; I think this speaks for itself. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6075-->
<!--Post: 6168--><!--Time: 1107563898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6168"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scbenson2001: It speaks for itself if you believe BTK is telling the truth. In the same letter he claims a ringing phone &#34;saved&#34; the kids. The phone could not have begun to ring as the wires were cut. Even if the phone had begun to ring, I don&#39;t understand why that would have necessarily scared BTK out of the house. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6168-->
<!--Post: 6175--><!--Time: 1107564884-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6175"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK didn&#39;t cut the wires.  He had originally planned on killing a neighbour if Shirley Vian&#39;s, but the woman wasn&#39;t home.  &#40;See the interview of Vian&#39;s son -- <a href="http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/news/nation/10817207.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/news/nati on/10817207.htm</a>  <BR> <BR>After knocking on that woman&#39;s door and getting no answer, he went over to Shirley Vian&#39;s house.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6175-->
<!--Post: 6184--><!--Time: 1107567907-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6184"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 5:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But BTK didn&#39;t cut the phone line to the neighbors house either so was she really the intended victim?  <BR> <BR>At the Otero&#39;s and at Nancy Fox&#39;s both phone lines were found cut from the outside of the house. <BR> <BR>At Anna Williams&#39; the phone line was cut but I haven&#39;t been able to find out if was cut from the outside or inside. <BR>At Vicki Wegerle&#39;s the phone line was not cut. <BR> <BR>At Kathryn Bright&#39;s I don&#39;t know if it was cut or not. <BR> <BR>Why cut some phone lines and not others?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6184-->
<!--Post: 6208--><!--Time: 1107580025-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6208"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 9:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK was armed and from Kevin Bright and the Vian boy&#39;s words, BTK was a cool customer. I just don&#39;t see a ringing phone suddenly terrifying him out of the house. BTK was armed; on the off-chance a phone ring would cause him to flee, he still could have shot the kids. The Vian-was-not-the-initial-target belief comes from the memory of a boy of eight. This needs to be factored into the credulity of his scenario. <BR> <BR><i>Why cut some phone lines and not others?</i> <BR>BTK wasn&#39;t as organized as believed? If he would do Vian because the neighbor wasn&#39;t home, then I don&#39;t know if BTK was organized at all. This Vian-because-neighbor-wasn&#39;t-home scenario reeks of disorganized behavior. All serial killers who aren&#39;t captured always have good luck; if BTK did what the Vian boy claims, he was one of the luckiest serial murderers ever. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6208-->
<!--Post: 6224--><!--Time: 1107601482-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6224"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 3:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was under the impression the lines were cut, also, but I am unable to find anything to substantiate that at present. <BR> <BR>But, I agree with George here, even if the phone did ring - why would that scare him off?  He would cut the lines to prevent calls &#39;out&#39; not in. <BR> <BR>Some have suggested that the &#39;bowling bag&#39; he carried was really one of those large mobile phone bags and that it was the phone that rang - summoning him to a job or something.   <BR> <BR>Charlie Otero&#39;s theory is very different - but may hold possibilities.  He feels that more than one person killed his family, in what was a &#39;hit&#39; of some sort - and that one killer branched off to do his own psycho killings because he liked it so much later. <BR> <BR>Everyone has discounted his theory - but he was a teen, not a young child like Vian, and he remembers events that led up to the kilings - events that made him feel his family was &#39;in trouble&#39;, or hiding from someone.   <BR> <BR>George - I watched the Vian son&#39;s interview - both parts.  I really don&#39;t believe there is anything credible he has to say.  He has lived a very hard life, is very bitter and emotional, but he has some real issues.  My heart goes out to him and his siblings, but he had a difficult time expressing his thoughts, he is very emotional, he has been in trouble with the law and his demeanor was not believable.  For his interview - he wore a black billed cap with a large white skull on the front and on either side were skeletal hands &#39;flipping the bird&#39;.  Pretty disrespectful - in my opinion.  BTK did a number on him - that&#39;s for sure. <BR> <BR>But that brings me to another question - were all the victims in the same type of social circle?  Were any wealthy victims chosen?   <BR> <BR>So far, &#40;I could be very wrong&#41; it seems as though the neighborhoods he hit were populated with the small, post WWII homes.  Not affluent areas.  He hit the working class.  That may be a natural thing - their homes being more penetrable.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6224-->
<!--Post: 6288--><!--Time: 1107660131-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Charlie O&#39;s theory isn&#39;t in the least impossible, nor do I find it absurd. I merely don&#39;t throw in with his theory at this time. Totally valid point that he was old enough, unlike the Vian boy, where chronological age isn&#39;t a factor regarding memory. But from what I have read, he was in shock on 1/15/74 - I also would have been - and I don&#39;t know that his specific memory can be considered without including this factor and maybe problems with the law apply here as well. He could still be right. No one has yet been apprehended for the crime. <BR> <BR>Great point about working class homes. Glad to stand corrected but I don&#39;t believe any of the victims were at all wealthy. Tippy, I&#39;m playing the percentages when I say I don&#39;t think there is a significant link among the victims, or at least a link which BTK knowingly used. I think they were random targets. But stats and percentages always have exceptions. Who knows??? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6288-->
<!--Post: 6477--><!--Time: 1107812621-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Awesome thread. I tend to steer toward the sex aspect of the crimes. I went and looked up about Bondage. I noticed the binding of the knees was fairly common. Gags also. What did he has about pillow case gags???<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6477-->
